# PHASE 10 — ADMIN PANEL: PROVIDER-WISE USER REGISTRATION ANALYTICS

The Admin Panel must display actual database-backed registration statistics.

This is a mandatory full-stack requirement.

### Required dashboard statistics

Display:

- Total registered users.
- Google-registered users.
- Facebook-registered users.
- Email/Password-registered users.
- Total active users, if supported by the existing account-status model.
- New registrations today.
- New registrations this week.
- New registrations this month.

### Important counting rules

Do not count login events as new registrations.

Do not count the same user multiple times simply because the user has multiple authentication providers.

Use the unified user identity and provider relationship data.

Define provider attribution consistently.

For example:

- Google registration count = unique NOVARA users whose initial registration provider was Google.
- Facebook registration count = unique NOVARA users whose initial registration provider was Facebook.
- Email registration count = unique NOVARA users whose initial registration method was Email/Password.

If a user later links another provider, do not silently change their original registration attribution.

If the existing project already has a different established attribution model, inspect it and implement a consistent, documented model without corrupting historical data.

### Admin analytics UI

Use the existing Admin Panel design system.

Provide:

- Summary cards.
- Provider-wise breakdown.
- Registration trends over time.
- Date-range filtering.
- Search and filtering where relevant.
- Pagination for user records.
- Loading states.
- Empty states.
- Error states.

Charts and summary numbers must be retrieved from real backend APIs and actual database queries.

Never use fake statistics or hardcoded chart data.

### Admin API requirements

Implement suitable authenticated and authorized endpoints, following existing project conventions.

Possible logical endpoints:

- GET /api/admin/users/authentication-stats
- GET /api/admin/users/registration-trends
- GET /api/admin/users/provider-breakdown

These are examples, not mandatory route names. Reuse existing routes where appropriate.

### Admin permissions

Only authorized administrators can access authentication analytics.

Regular users must not be able to access admin statistics or other users' private authentication information.

Enforce permissions on the backend, not just by hiding frontend menu items.

